<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Turin (1381)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1381">1381</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-chioggia">War of Chioggia</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> was concluded in August 1381 through the mediation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-vi-count-of-savoy">Amadeus VI of Savoy</a> and ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-chioggia">War of Chioggia</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> and their allies. Venice gave up Treviso, recognised Hungarian rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> and agreed that the disputed island of Tenedos would be evacuated. Neither city gained a decisive advantage, but Venice emerged as the stronger power in the following decades.</p></div>
